<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flores, Guatemala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flores is a town on an island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-peten-itza">Lake Petén Itzá</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. It stands on the site of Nojpetén, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itza-people">Itza Maya</a> kingdom, which the Spanish conquered in 1697. Linked to the shore by a causeway, it is a base for visitors to Tikal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flores-guatemala.jpg" alt="Flores, Guatemala" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Francisco · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flores_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
